#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Unified experiment and analysis pipeline for the manuscript:

    Reliable Internal Training Diagnostics for Deep Neural Networks:
    A Multi-Seed Study of Layer-Wise Weight-Update Dynamics

The script keeps the official test sets untouched, creates a stratified
validation split only from the official training set, runs a reproducible
multi-seed experiment matrix, records external and internal training metrics,
and produces publication-ready CSV tables and figures.

Install
-------
python -m pip install torch torchvision numpy pandas scipy scikit-learn \
    matplotlib seaborn tqdm statsmodels

Paper run (120 runs)
--------------------
python internal_dynamics_study.py all --output results_paper --preset paper \
    --seeds 0 1 2 3 4 --epochs 30 --device auto

Small end-to-end check
----------------------
python internal_dynamics_study.py all --output results_smoke --preset smoke \
    --seeds 0 --epochs 2 --device auto

Resume an interrupted run
-------------------------
Run the same command again. Completed run JSON files are detected and skipped.

Analyze existing completed runs only
------------------------------------
python internal_dynamics_study.py analyze --output results_paper

Important output files
----------------------
results_paper/tables/run_metrics.csv
results_paper/tables/epoch_metrics.csv
results_paper/tables/layer_epoch_metrics.csv
results_paper/tables/config_summary.csv
results_paper/tables/early_diagnostics.csv
results_paper/tables/early_predictor_comparison.csv
results_paper/tables/spearman_correlations.csv
results_paper/tables/fixed_effects_models.csv
results_paper/figures/*.png and *.pdf

The code intentionally uses balanced binary tasks so that failure definitions
and cross-dataset comparisons are interpretable:
  * MNIST: digits 4 versus 9
  * Fashion-MNIST: Pullover (2) versus Shirt (6)
  * CIFAR-10: Cat (3) versus Dog (5)
"""

